 us\nPostgraduate\nTaught programmes\nPostgraduate Research\nMeet us\nResearch\nResearch centres\nOur Research Seminars\nPostdoctoral fellowship opportunities\nStatistics and Data Science Clinic\nOur Community\nMathematics Society\nOur building\nEquality, Diversity and Inclusion\nMaths Ambassadors\nMental Health and Wellbeing Group (Me + We)\nPeople\nAcademic staff\nEmeritus staff\nResearch staff\nResearch students\nProfessional Services\nNews and Events\nNews\nEvents\nAlumni\nBreadcrumb\nSchool of Mathematical Sciences\nPostgraduate\nPostgraduate Research\nEntry requirements\nIn this section\nPostgraduate Research\nPhD projects\nCurrent PhD projects\nCombinatorics, Algebra and Number Theory PhD Projects\nComplex Systems PhD Projects\nGeometry, Analysis and Gravitation PhD Projects\nProbability, Statistics and Data Science PhD Project\nChina Scholarship Council Projects\nFees and funding\nPast PGR awards\nEntry requirements\nApplication process\nTimeline for SMS PhD students\nPGR training\nOur PhD students\nOur PhD graduates\nPhD Information Session 2026\nEntry requirements\nRequirements for each PhD project vary but generally we are looking for applicants who hold, or expect to receive:\nA first-class honours degree in Mathematics or Statistics or the equivalent qualification from an overseas institution. If your qualifications are not from a UK university, QMUL also considers recognised equivalent qualifications from accredited overseas institutions and equivalent professional qualification.\nIdeally you should have a more advanced qualification such as MSci, MMath or MSc, in which case we expect at least an upper second in your undergraduate degree with a merit in your postgraduate degree.\nSpecific entry requirements or experience required will be listed on the relevant project page where applicable.\nInternational and European qualifications\nPlease see the Queen Mary University of London International pages for information on recognised equivalent qualifications specific to your country.\nAlternatively, for advice on your qualification equivalency, please contact research-admissions@qmul.ac.uk.\nEnglish language requirements\nAll students must meet Queen Mary's English language requirements. The minimum level required for entry to our postgraduate programmes is as follows:\nAcademic IELTS: 6.5 overall, with a 6.0 in all categories.\nOther qualifications can also be considered; please see the Queen Mary English language requirements guidelines for further information.\nStudents that have yet to take an English proficiency test may still apply and may recieve a conditional offer subject to meeting the minimum English language requirements.\nEnglish language and study skills at Queen Mary\nThe Queen Mary Language Centre offers a range of pre-sessional and in-sessional English language courses for students who have not quite reached the required standard of language ability, or for those wishing to improve their English language and study skills.\nFooter navigation\nAccommodation\nAlumni\nSchools and Institutes\nCareers and Employability\nCollaborate with us\nContact\nEvents\nGlobal\nHow to find us\nInternational students\nJobs\nLibrary\nMyQMUL\nNew students\nNews\nOrder a prospectus\nOur brand\nParents\nProfessional services departments\nPublic Engagement\nQMplus\nStaff directory\nStaff intranet\nStrategy 2030\nStudents' Union\nTeachers\nTerm dates\nTrade Union Facility Time\nAccessibility\nDisclaimer\nPrivacy and cookies\nSite map\nModern Slavery Statement\nSupplier fraud alert\nOFS Data\nContact the university\nQueen Mary University of London\nMile End Road\nLondon E1 4NS\n+44 (0) 20 7882 5555\nBack to top\nEdit this page", "links": [["honeypot link", "https://4xvmpmomo3.execute-api.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/ProdStage"], ["Skip to main content", "https://www.qmul.ac.uk/maths/postgraduate/postgraduate-research/entry-requirements/#main-content"], ["", "https://www.qmul.ac.uk/maths/postgraduate/postgraduate-research/entry-requ